  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: No experiments have been completed, so there is zero prior information about which design choices (modality, encoder, profile strategy, aggregation, fusion) matter or interact. 2) What this tests: config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most standard baseline in the design space. It establishes a clean performance floor using a well-understood dimensionality reduction (PCA-2000) on the RNA modality alone, with no confounding from image processing, multiprofile aggregation, or fusion. 3) Why it is the best first experiment: Under a limited budget, the first experiment should maximize interpretability of all subsequent comparisons. Every later configuration can be framed as 'what does adding X (image, multiprofile, transformer aggregation, fusion, alternative encoder) contribute relative to this baseline?' Starting with the simplest, most established configuration avoids conflating multiple novel design choices in one run and gives the clearest signal for the next round of targeted ablations."
